# Archon of Emeria: "Each player can't cast more than one spell each turn" binds its own controller too (CR 101.2), the count
# starts over every turn, and "Nonbasic lands your opponents control enter tapped" leaves a basic land untapped.
# Turn 2: Bot2 casts Sol Ring and then Archon (three spells in a turn, all before the Archon is out: no limit yet).
# Turn 3: Bot1's basic Plains enters untapped (the nonbasic land entering tapped is in the existing scenarios), and Bot1's
# second spell is refused beside its first, allowed. Turn 4: Bot2 may cast one Mox, and the second is refused. Turn 6:
# the count is fresh and Bot2 casts the second Mox.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Plains x4
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Sol Ring
Archon of Emeria
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Plains x3
Plains x8

[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Archon of Emeria.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield = Plains; Mox Pearl; Sol Ring; Archon of Emeria
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
? Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Tapped = false
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Tapped = false
! Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
! Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Tapped = false
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Tapped = false
